---
import PublicLayout from "../layouts/PublicLayout.astro";
import clubInfo from "../data/clubInfo.json";

const lastUpdated = "March 9, 2026";
---

<PublicLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - Mini-THON"
  description="Learn how GMHS Mini-THON uses newsletter, analytics, and member-login data on gmhsminithon.org."
>
  <section class="policy-shell">
    <div class="policy-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
      <h1>How we use your information</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This policy explains what information GMHS Mini-THON may process through
        gmhsminithon.org, how we use it, and the third-party services involved
        in running the site.
      </p>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      <p>
        Privacy laws vary by location, so this page is intended to explain the
        site's current data practices in a clear and transparent way. If you
        need a legal determination about compliance requirements for your school
        or organization, you should also have this policy reviewed by an
        appropriate administrator or legal advisor.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>Information we may receive</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Newsletter signup details:</strong> if newsletter signup is enabled,
            we may receive the email address you submit.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Member portal authentication data:</strong> when you sign in with
            Shoo, we verify your Shoo identity token and use your Shoo user ID (`pairwise_sub`)
            to decide whether you can access the members portal.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Basic technical data:</strong> our hosting and application infrastructure
            may process information such as request metadata and performance information
            needed to serve the site securely and reliably.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How we use that information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To operate the public website and member portal.</li>
          <li>
            To verify whether a Shoo-authenticated user is approved for
            member-only access.
          </li>
          <li>
            To send newsletter updates if you choose to subscribe when that
            feature is active.
          </li>
          <li>
            To monitor site performance, diagnose problems, and protect the site
            from misuse.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Member portal details</h2>
        <p>
          The members portal uses Shoo for sign-in. After Shoo authenticates
          you, this site verifies your Shoo token on the server and checks your
          Shoo user ID against a private approval list maintained by GMHS
          Mini-THON administrators.
        </p>
        <p>
          That approval list may be stored in server environment variables
          and/or a private Google Sheet CSV source configured by administrators.
          If your account is not yet approved, the login flow may show your Shoo
          user ID so you can share it with an admin for approval.
        </p>
        <p>
          If access is granted, the site stores a short-lived session cookie so
          you can use the members portal without signing in on every page load.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Shoo</strong> is used to authenticate member portal users.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>EmailOctopus</strong> is used for newsletter subscriptions when
            that feature is enabled.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Vercel</strong> hosts the site and provides analytics and performance
            tooling used to understand site reliability and usage.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Sheets</strong> may be used by administrators as a private
            source for approved Shoo user IDs.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          When you interact with third-party services through this site, their
          own terms and privacy policies may also apply. We encourage you to
          review those policies directly before submitting information to those
          services.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Sharing and retention</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell personal information. We only share data with the
          service providers needed to operate the site and its features.
        </p>
        <p>
          Information is kept only as long as needed for the relevant purpose,
          such as maintaining the member approval list, keeping a newsletter
          subscription active, or preserving short-lived session and diagnostic
          data needed to operate the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
        <p>
          The members portal uses a short-lived session cookie after successful
          sign-in so authenticated members can access protected pages. Vercel's
          analytics and performance tooling may also use service-side telemetry
          and similar technologies to measure reliability and site usage.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your privacy choices and rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live, you may have rights to request access to,
          correction of, deletion of, or restriction of certain personal data.
          You may also be able to unsubscribe from email updates at any time.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can choose not to use the members portal or newsletter signup. If
          you want to ask about, update, or remove information associated with
          this site, contact us at
          <a href={`mailto:${clubInfo.contact.email}`}
            >{clubInfo.contact.email}</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
          This site is intended for the GMHS Mini-THON school community and is
          not designed to knowingly collect personal information from children
          under 13 without appropriate authorization. If you believe personal
          information from a child under 13 has been submitted in error, contact
          us so we can review and address it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy from time to time to reflect changes to the
          site, its services, or our data practices. When we make a material
          update, we will revise the "Last updated" date on this page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Additional legal notices</h2>
        <p>
          This policy is provided to explain current site practices in plain
          language. It is not legal advice and should not be treated as a
          substitute for professional legal review.
        </p>
        <p>
          This site may contain links to third-party websites and services that
          GMHS Mini-THON does not control. We are not responsible for the
          content, security, or privacy practices of those external services.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</PublicLayout>

<style>
  .policy-shell {
    width: min(100%, 900px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 1.5rem 5rem;
  }

  .policy-card {
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    border-radius: 24px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
    padding: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--brand-sky);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-900);
  }

  .lede,
  .meta,
  p,
  li {
    color: var(--ink-700);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .meta {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-900);
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--brand-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
